-- title:
--   Hecke inputs at the degeneracy roof for invertible q
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $N$ and $q$ be natural numbers, both nonzero, with $q$ prime, and assume that the intermediate field $k(j,\;j_N,\;j_q,\;j_{Nq})$ of the field of formal Laurent series over $k$ generated by the four $q$-expansion generators `jqModC k`, `jqNModC k N`, `jqNModC k q` and `jqNModC k (N * q)` has principal divisors, that is: every nonzero element $f$ of that field admits a divisor $D$ (a finitely supported integer-valued function on the places of the field over $k$) with $D(v) = v.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at every place $v$ and with $\deg D = 0$. Assume further that $q$ is invertible in $k$, i.e. $(q : k) \neq 0$. Then the predicate `HeckeInputsFibre k N q` holds: there exist a witness that the above roof field has principal divisors, a witness that the underlying ring homomorphism of the degeneracy leg `heckeBetaC k N q` is integral, and a witness that the underlying ring homomorphism of `heckeAlphaC k N q` is integral, such that the induced additive endomorphism `heckeDivFibre` of the divisor group of `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, namely the correspondence attached to those two legs, sends degree-zero divisors to degree-zero divisors and principal divisors to principal divisors, hence descends to $\mathrm{Pic}^0$.
--
--   This assembles, in closed form, the hypotheses needed to realise the Hecke correspondence $T_q$ on the degree-zero divisor class group of the modular curve of level $N$ over a field in which $q$ is invertible, the input being a single arithmetic condition on $q$ together with principality of divisors on the four-generator roof field. It is the form in which the construction is invoked downstream, in the analysis of component groups and of specialisations of places under the Hecke action.
